What the data is made of

- Our own files (the map, the method, the gap pages, the contracts, the tools) are MIT.
- References link to and pin their sources: Microsoft Learn pages by their git_commit_id and
  updated_at, GitHub sources by commit. A claim is one line in our own words, with an ID; no table
  or text from a source is copied.
- The Azure Virtual Desktop review checklist is cited by item short ID (such as A01.01), never
  reproduced. Cloud Adoption Framework content (CC BY 4.0) is linked, never reproduced.
- A reader who reproduces a source's text must follow that source's license, not this one.
- Third-party products appear only as categories, never by name. Liquidware, the one partner the
  family names, appears only in this notice and the partner rule.
- No tenant, customer, user or machine data is in the map.

tests/public-ids.txt and tests/public-ipv4.txt list the published Microsoft identifiers and
addresses the leak scan allows, so anyone can rerun it on a release.
